# No Unsolicited Builds

Never run build or verification commands on your own initiative. This includes:

- `xcodebuild`, `swift build`, `swift test`
- `npm run build`, `npm test`, and equivalents in other toolchains
- Any long-running compile, test-suite, or CI-style command

Make the code changes and stop. State what you changed and let the user build or run it themselves.

Only run these commands when the user explicitly asks (e.g. "build it", "run the tests", "verify this compiles") or when a plan they approved lists verification as a step.
